		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_CULTURE">
			<Text>The [B]Cultural Victory[/B] is awarded to a leader when they achieve cultural dominance against all other leaders. This dominance is measured by [B]Tourism[/B] and comes from the following sources:[NN][BLIST]
				[LI][B]Natural Wonders[/B]: 10 points when at least one tile is improved
				[LI][B]Wonders[/B]: 4 points in Antiquity, 8 points in Exploration, and 12 points in Modern
				[LI][B]Displayed Relics[/B]: 3 points
				[LI][B]Displayed Artifacts[/B]: 5 points
				[LI][B]Celebrations[/B]: 2 points per Age after Researching Entertainment
				[LI][B]Unique Improvements[/B]: 1 point for every type of Unique Improvement in a Settlement (4 points in Settlements connected by Rail after Researching Industrialization's Mastery in Modern Age)
				[LI][B]Unique Buildings[/B]: 1 point in Antiquity, 2 points in Exploration, and 4 points in Modern (7 points in Settlements with an Aerodrome after Researching Flight's Mastery)
				[LI][B]Resort Towns[/B]: 4 points per Breathtaking tile when at least 7 tiles are Breathtaking in Modern after Researching Globalism's Mastery
				[LI][B]Certain Triumphs and Civics[/B]: Varies
				[/LIST][NN]Note that Wonders captured from other leaders are worth greatly reduced points.</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_MILITARY">
			<Text>The [B]Military Victory[/B] is awarded to a leader when they achieve military dominance against all other leaders. This dominance is measured by [B]Dominion[/B], which is primarily a measure of [B]Settlements[/B].[NN]Each Settlement you control is worth [B]4 Dominion[/B]. Settlements can be worth additional Dominion as follows:[NN][BLIST]
				[LI][B]Original Capital[/B]: +4 points
				[LI][B]Distant Lands[/B]: +1 point
				[LI][B]Captured[/B]: +1 point
				[LI][B]Captured from Ideological Opponent[/B]: +2 points[/LIST]</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_SCIENTIFIC">
			<Text>The [B]Scientific Victory[/B] is awarded to a leader when they win the [B]Space Race[/B]. This requires earning 100 [B]Innovation[/B] and having an active Launch Pad.
				[NN]Innovation is earned through many different ways. The two primary ways to earn them are by researching [B]Tech Masteries[/B] and completing [B]Projects[/B]. You can unlock these Projects by researching advanced Techs in each Age, then you can produce them in any City that meets the requirements. The Masteries and Projects vary in point values.
				[NN]Certain Science-based Wonders provide 3 points, and you can earn an additional +1 point for each [B]Codex[/B] displayed in a [B]Great Work Slot[/B] during the Antiquity Age.  Some Triumphs in the Modern Age also provide Innovation.</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_ECONOMIC">
			<Text>
				The [B]Economic Victory[/B] is awarded to a leader when they achieve economic dominance against all other leaders. This dominance is measured by [B]GDP[/B]. The following contribute to your GDP each turn:[NN][BLIST]
				[LI][B]Gold Buildings[/B]: +2 GDP per turn for each Gold Building from the current Age after Researching Currency.
				[LI][B]City Resources and Bonus Resources[/B]: +1 GDP per turn for each City and Bonus Resource assigned to a City (not a Town) after Researching The Wheel.
				[LI][B]Imported Resources[/B]: +1 additional GDP per turn for each Resource imported via a [B]Trade Route[/B] and assigned to a City (not a Town) after Researching Skilled Trades.
				[LI][B]Treasure Convoys[/B]: 20 GDP per Cargo for each returned Treasure Convoy. This amount scales by Game Speed.
				[LI][B]Factory Resources[/B]: +3 GDP per turn for each Factory Resource assigned to a City or Town.[/LIST][NN]Certain Triumphs in the Modern Age also provide GDP.</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_SCORE_HEADER_1">
			<Text>How Score is determined</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_SCORE_BODY_1">
			<Text>[B]The following major elements are factored in this order:[B][NN][NLIST][LI]How many turns you have been in a Victory Countdown over all Victories.[LI]Your placement among all active Victory types.[LI]How many major Triumphs you have completed over the course of a game.[/LIST]</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_SCORE_HEADER_2">
			<Text>Details</Text>
		</Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_VICTORIES_RULES_SCORE_BODY_2">
			<Text>[B]The individual elements are added together to give your score.[B][NN][NLIST][LI]Victory Countdown turns times 1000.[LI]1000 minus 10 times your current placement in all Victory types.[LI]The sum total of all major Triumphs you have completed.[/LIST]</Text>
		</Row>
